WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.690
There is something deeply unsettling about
an old house at night.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:09.280
What is beautiful, if a bit worse for wear,
during the day can take on a sinister cast

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.400
once the sun goes down.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.710
The moan of the wind outside, the creak of
the floorboards, the scraping of a branch

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.380
against a window.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:23.050
Maybe one of these sounds jolts you awake
in the dead of night, eyes opening to a room

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.739
full of shadows turned twisted and eerie in
the darkness.

00:00:26.739 --> 00:00:29.619
Of course, it’s probably nothing supernatural.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:33.390
Just an old house settling, mixed with your
own paranoia.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:38.420
But sometimes, every so often, it is something
more.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.170
Sometimes you’re not as alone in an old
house as you think you are.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:48.839
That’s certainly the case if you ever find
yourself staying in SCP-2696, also known as

00:00:48.839 --> 00:00:52.609
the Haunted Victorian Mansion of Dark Peak.

00:00:52.609 --> 00:00:58.379
In 1869, wealthy and renowned industrialist
- and scholar of the occult - Henry Percival

00:00:58.379 --> 00:01:04.080
Rosyth built a stately home, known as Rosyth
Hall, to house him, his wife Clara, and any

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.490
children they might have in the future.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:11.790
It was constructed to provide Henry with ample
space to conduct his arcane research, Clara

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:15.980
with a beautiful sitting room and a flower
garden to tend, and their future children

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.820
with lots of space to play and run around
as they grew.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:25.820
After an uneventful year in the house, Clara
gave birth to two baby boys, named Edgar and

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:26.820
Miles.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.290
For a time, the family was happy there.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:34.670
Unfortunately, this happiness was to be short-lived,
as the grim specter of death soon began to

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:36.810
loom over Rosyth Hall.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:43.090
In January of 1873, Clara was overcome with
a sudden fever and died in her bed.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:47.650
This loss pushed the already eccentric Henry
over the edge, and he began making strange

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.770
changes to the house’s interior structure.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:56.840
He added hallways that led to dead ends, strangely
angled floors, and twisting corners, turning

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:01.340
a once comfortable and lived-in home into
something unrecognizable.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:07.200
In August of that same year, Henry’s children,
Edgar and Miles, also suddenly passed away,

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.460
leaving Henry alone at his estate as he continued
his descent into madness.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:16.990
He kept modifying the house, expanding from
the mansion’s library and tower to the rest

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:18.440
of the building's rooms.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:23.050
Henry’s days were spent supervising the
construction around the house, refusing to

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:27.810
let the workers carry on without his strict
oversight, worried that otherwise his vision

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.490
would be corrupted.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:33.970
His nights were spent sleepless, as he worked
away in the tower and in the nursery on the

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:35.370
second floor.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:39.630
No one was permitted to witness his work during
the night, but his household staff complained

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:44.250
of strange sounds, flashing lights, and strange
whispers.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:48.810
Many were so unsettled by these sounds, and
Mr. Rosyth’s erratic behavior, that they

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.700
quit their jobs without notice.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.930
A wise choice, given the circumstances.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.950
As his staff dwindled, so too did Henry Rosyth’s
already fragile grip on reality.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.010
His requests for materials became more and
more imposing.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:08.630
He demanded 200 kilograms of ground stone
from Isle of Anglesey in Wales, and 37 meters

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:14.360
of pipes made from an amalgam of mercury and
copper, among other unconventional materials.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:20.230
But Rosyth still had money to burn, and no
family to spend it on anymore, so his every

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:24.170
strange request was accommodated - for a time,
anyway.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:30.180
In June of 1876, exhausted and unsettled by
the long hours of work, the ever increasingly

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:35.270
strange projects, and the unusual, supernatural
phenomena around the house, the remainder

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.950
of Rosyth’s workers quit.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:41.550
He then fired all of his household staff,
with the exception of his loyal housekeeper,

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.200
and resumed his work in solitude.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.510
Though the specifics of just what Mr Forsyth
was trying to achieve would likely have gone

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:53.610
to the grave with him, some of his diary entries
were recovered from the house, and they provide

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:58.210
a peek into his motives, and the nature of
the mansion’s anomalous activity.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:02.440
After the death of his wife and children,
he became obsessed with the concept of the

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:07.380
“mind-made body,” the notion that having
a memory so strong that, if given the proper

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:11.510
energetic conditions, it could take on corporeal
form.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:17.139
His theory was, if a memory is engraved permanently
in the mind, it could then take on a permanent

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:19.909
physical and energetic manifestation.

00:04:19.909 --> 00:04:24.210
He began to experiment with this concept,
determined to bring back a form of his wife

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.699
and children by any means necessary.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:30.590
A noble pursuit that paved the way to madness.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:34.590
It is during this process that he began to
remodel the house in order to provide the

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:38.529
ideal energetic conditions for his memories
to be made material.

00:04:38.529 --> 00:04:43.280
Eventually, his notes devolved into nonsense
and the pages were covered with geometric

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.050
equations and blood.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.940
His final entry reads: “The children still
speak in her voice.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:51.330
I fear I might be going mad.”

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:56.379
It is true that he may have been losing his
grip on sanity toward the end of his experiments,

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:59.629
but his work undeniably filled the house with
something.

00:04:59.629 --> 00:05:04.180
It was not long before reports of strange
sights and sounds around the Rosyth home reached

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:07.849
the ears of those trained to investigate such
matters.

00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:11.589
The house, and its anomalous nature, were
initially discovered by Jitinder Jaishankar;

00:05:11.589 --> 00:05:17.809
an occultist and investigator employed by
the Royal Foundation for the Secure Containment

00:05:17.809 --> 00:05:21.159
of the Paranormal - or RFSCP.

00:05:21.159 --> 00:05:26.370
He wrote the first official report on the
house in 1876, after investigating multiple

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.759
rumors of ghostly sightings around the house.

00:05:28.759 --> 00:05:34.409
He and his team, a married pair of ghost hunters
named The Bartons, arrived at the Rosyth home

00:05:34.409 --> 00:05:36.749
with a sense of apprehension.

00:05:36.749 --> 00:05:41.120
They were ushered through the door by a housekeeper,
who made the eerie promise that Henry Rosyth

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.449
would be with them shortly.

00:05:42.449 --> 00:05:46.979
When the master of the house came to greet
them, the investigative team was shocked at

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.039
his appearance.

00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:53.800
He was gaunt, almost skeletal, with dark,
deep-set eyes bleary from entirely too long

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.830
without sleep.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:06:00.349
He looked as if he had aged a hundred years
in the few years since his wife’s death.

00:06:00.349 --> 00:06:05.210
The team stayed the night in the house, experiencing
a restless and nightmare-addled sleep until

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.789
2:30 AM, when the investigative work was to
begin.

00:06:08.789 --> 00:06:13.539
They descended down to the main hall of the
house, where a large black door was all that

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:16.240
stood between them and the unknown.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:20.919
It opened with a bone-deep groan, as if to
warn them not to enter.

00:06:20.919 --> 00:06:23.499
But still, they stepped inside.

00:06:23.499 --> 00:06:27.759
Once they crossed the threshold, they were
greeted with odd angles, a garish array of

00:06:27.759 --> 00:06:32.139
colors and materials, and bewilderingly high
ceilings.

00:06:32.139 --> 00:06:35.949
All to Mr. Rosyth’s very demanding specifications,
of course.

00:06:35.949 --> 00:06:41.939
He’d spared no expense in making his nonsensical
nightmare house an unsettling reality.

00:06:41.939 --> 00:06:46.089
The Bartons presented dowsing rods, which
they used to measure spiritual activity in

00:06:46.089 --> 00:06:47.089
the room.

00:06:47.089 --> 00:06:51.770
At first, nothing happened, but soon the dowsing
rods began to spark viciously, and a sudden

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:54.740
gust of wind blew out all of the candles in
the room.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:07:00.069
There was nothing but darkness, and a sudden
sense of a heavy presence amongst them.

00:07:00.069 --> 00:07:04.439
The Bartons dropped to the floor, with Mrs.
Barton leaking blood from her mouth, and Dr.

00:07:04.439 --> 00:07:06.300
Barton convulsing violently.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:11.889
The presence grew stronger, and though it
did not speak it was unmistakable who it was:

00:07:11.889 --> 00:07:14.749
it was the deceased Clara Rosyth.

00:07:14.749 --> 00:07:19.710
Jaishankar fled the manor, dragging his unconscious
companions out as fast as he could.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:24.949
Once safely away from the mansion, he immediately
contacted the RFSCP… well as quickly as

00:07:24.949 --> 00:07:27.419
one can when communicating by telegram.

00:07:27.419 --> 00:07:31.879
A second team was sent to investigate the
house in the following days, but when they

00:07:31.879 --> 00:07:34.750
arrived, Henry Rosyth could not be found.

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:40.050
There was no sign of a struggle, no body,
he had simply vanished.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.990
He was never seen again.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:46.679
The SCP Foundation has an official record
of two separate incorporeal entities that

00:07:46.679 --> 00:07:51.759
dwell within the walls of SCP-2696.

00:07:51.759 --> 00:07:56.979
The first, SCP-2696-1, appears to be the ghost,
or the memory, energetic signature, whatever

00:07:56.979 --> 00:07:59.800
you wish to call it, of Clara Rosyth.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:04.159
The apparition is the one that Jitinder Jaishankar
and the Bartons encountered.

00:08:04.159 --> 00:08:09.460
She is translucent and intangible, and most
frequently appears in the form of Clara as

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.379
a young mother, at the pinnacle of her good
health.

00:08:12.379 --> 00:08:17.659
She has also occasionally taken on several
inhuman forms, including a wilting plumeria

00:08:17.659 --> 00:08:21.879
bush, and a disturbing column of bone, muscle,
and flesh.

00:08:21.879 --> 00:08:27.310
Exposure to the Clara entity has a pronounced
negative effect on anyone who comes near her.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:34.050
People that come within several feet of SCP-2696-1
have reported mild visual and auditory hallucinations,

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:38.380
such as creeping shadows and whispering voices
chanting in foreign languages.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:44.910
There have also been reports of amnesia, fainting,
seizures, bleeding from the nose, mouth, and

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:50.660
ears, and, in the most severe cases, dissociative
episodes that result in a complete loss of

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:51.660
identity.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:55.090
Many of these physical side effects are thought
to be the result of the massive amounts of

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:58.940
radiation that have been measured being given
off by the entity.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:06.100
The second entity in the house, known as SCP-2696-2,
is actually two entities that always seem

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.019
to come as a pair.

00:09:08.019 --> 00:09:14.550
Known as 2A and 2B, these are the skeletons
of Miles and Edgar Rosyth, the deceased children

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:15.800
of Clara and Henry.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:21.019
They are located inside of the nursery, which
is inaccessible to outsiders, with a door

00:09:21.019 --> 00:09:25.420
that seems able to seal itself shut at will
and keep researchers out.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:30.100
The two skeletons are largely inactive, remaining
on the floor of the nursery in the fetal position

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.449
at nearly all times.

00:09:32.449 --> 00:09:36.819
They only become active during periods of
extreme activity from the Clara entity.

00:09:36.819 --> 00:09:41.430
When Clara is especially active, and attempting
to leave her usual domain in the house’s

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:45.779
tower, the skeletons have been reported to
wrestle and play with each other, dance around

00:09:45.779 --> 00:09:50.579
the room, or stand at the door to the nursery,
appearing to be waiting for something.

00:09:50.579 --> 00:09:58.570
On one notable occasion though, on June 12th,
1990, both instances of SCP-2696-2 were able

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:02.089
to actually leave the nursery and travel elsewhere
in the house.

00:10:02.089 --> 00:10:07.010
A series of massive lightning strikes raised
the energy levels in the house, and Clara’s

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:09.970
radiation levels suddenly spiked significantly.

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:15.230
Surge protectors placed in the house failed,
and Clara became more active than usual, transforming

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:19.240
into a swirling dark mass that emitted an
ear splitting shriek.

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:23.709
The front door of the mansion slammed itself
shut and refused to open, trapping the research

00:10:23.709 --> 00:10:26.149
team who were present at the time.

00:10:26.149 --> 00:10:32.399
They were only able to exit after SCP-2696-2A
and 2B were spotted leaving the nursery.

00:10:32.399 --> 00:10:36.170
Hand in hand, they approached Clara and opened
their arms to her.

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:41.580
Pacified, perhaps by some distant echo of
a mother’s love, the entity quieted, and

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:44.190
the Foundation team was finally able to leave.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:49.180
It is still unknown how 2A and 2B were able
to leave the nursery, but there have not been

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:51.839
any incidents of this level since.

00:10:51.839 --> 00:10:56.750
Currently, the Dark Peak mansion remains standing,
and is largely untouched from how its creator

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:57.750
left it.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:02.940
The SCP Foundation maintains a strict perimeter
of one square kilometer around the house,

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:05.640
and no civilians are permitted to cross it.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:10.430
Not only is the building restricted for civilians,
most SCP Foundation personnel are also forbidden

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:12.430
from entering the house.

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:17.829
Some of the only ones who are allowed inside
are a special class of SCP Foundation personnel,

00:11:17.829 --> 00:11:24.600
Experimental Containment Research Group, or
ECRG, and MTF Theta-77, nicknamed "Who You

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:25.740
Gonna Call?"

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:30.269
Given what was learned in the 1990 activation
event, it is apparent that the containment

00:11:30.269 --> 00:11:36.860
procedures have a rate of failure that does
not adequately contain SCP-2696-1, and according

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:42.040
to the containment file, there is a 47% chance
of Clara breaching containment completely

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.590
by 2030.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:48.129
Catherine Steadman once wrote: “Houses aren’t
haunted, people are.”

00:11:48.129 --> 00:11:52.329
Henry Rosyth was so haunted by the loss of
his beloved wife and children that he could

00:11:52.329 --> 00:11:56.220
not stand to live in his big empty house all
alone.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:12:01.550
Henry Rosyth may be long gone, but his attempts
to grasp at that which was long gone before

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:04.810
him have forever changed the house he built.

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:10.760
His grief, his pain, his energy, filled the
house with echoes of his loved ones, and,

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:16.519
as pain often does when left untreated, it
began to fester and turn foul.

00:12:16.519 --> 00:12:22.930
Dr. Henry Rosyth was a deeply haunted man,
and now his haunted house is all that remains

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:23.930
of him.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:27.029
Now go check out “SCP-1730 - What Happened
to Site-13?

00:12:27.029 --> 00:12:33.120
The Full Story Compilation” and “SCP-1337
- The Hitchhiker” for anomalies that’ll

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:33.970
chill you to the bone!

